# LF everywhere, on every OS: the shell scripts run under bash (also Git Bash on Windows, issue #49) and on the Echo's
# mksh, and device.conf, *.rc, sepolicy.rules and the rest are sourced or pushed to it as they are.  A Windows clone
# with Git's default core.autocrlf=true got CRLF, and bash fails on that; mksh takes a CR as part of the word
# (`D=/system/hassmic\r` breaks the boot scripts).
* text=auto eol=lf
*.raw binary
*.mp3 binary
*.pub binary
*.key binary
*.bundle binary
*.sig binary
